# Zustand Stores

## Boundary (what belongs in a store)

Zustand holds ONLY ephemeral client/UI state: open modals, drawers, selected filters, row selections, theme, wizard step. Server data ALWAYS goes through TanStack Query feature hooks — never mirror fetched data into a store (see web-architecture rule).

## Location & naming

- Cross-cutting: `src/shared/stores/<name>-store.ts`.
- Feature-scoped: `src/features/<feature>/stores/<name>-store.ts`.
- Export the hook as `use<Name>Store` (e.g. `useUIStore`).

## Store shape

Type the state, group fields first then actions, and use functional `set` for derived updates. Keep each store small and single-purpose — split by concern rather than building one mega-store.

```typescript
type UIState = {
  mobileNavOpen: boolean;            // state first
  setMobileNavOpen: (open: boolean) => void;  // then actions
  toggleMobileNav: () => void;
};

export const useUIStore = create<UIState>((set) => ({
  mobileNavOpen: false,
  setMobileNavOpen: (open) => set({ mobileNavOpen: open }),
  toggleMobileNav: () => set((s) => ({ mobileNavOpen: !s.mobileNavOpen })),
}));
```

For large stores, use the slices pattern: typed `StateCreator` slices combined in one `create`.

## Easy data fetching (selectors)

Always select the narrowest slice, and export atomic selector hooks so a component reads state with one import.

```typescript
// GOOD — narrow selector, only re-renders when this field changes
const open = useUIStore((s) => s.mobileNavOpen);

// GOOD — ship ready-made selector hooks next to the store
export const useMobileNavOpen = () => useUIStore((s) => s.mobileNavOpen);

// BAD — selecting the whole store re-renders on every change
const store = useUIStore();
```

- Selecting multiple fields/objects? Use `useShallow` to avoid re-render churn:
  `const { a, b } = useUIStore(useShallow((s) => ({ a: s.a, b: s.b })));`
- Read outside React with `useUIStore.getState()`; never subscribe in non-React code.

## Actions

Mutate state only through named actions inside the store — never call `set` from components. Actions are stable references, safe in effect/callback dependency arrays.

## Middleware

- Wrap with `devtools` (pass a store `name`) for debuggability.
- Use `persist` only for durable UI prefs (theme, sidebar collapsed) with an explicit `name` and `partialize`. Never persist server data or transient flags.

## Anti-patterns

- Storing TanStack Query results in a store.
- `const store = useUIStore()` (selecting everything).
- Business logic in components instead of store actions.
